                "message": "Fix crash when a C and/or is nested in a Python object and/or\n\nIn \"(x > 0 and not a and not b) if c else True\", the nested\n\"not a and not b\" kept its C bint type while the outer and/or became\na Python object. Its values were then cast straight to PyObject* in\nthe generated C code. This was only repaired when the caller ran\ncoerce_to() on the whole expression, which CondExprNode and comparisons\nskip when the type already matches.\n\nConvert a nested and/or when one of the two is a C value and the other\na Python object. Nested C values of another C type are already\nconverted when they are stored in the result, and operands that cannot\nbe converted, such as C pointers, are left alone, since they are still\nvalid in a boolean context.\n\nFixes https://github.com/cython/cython/issues/7472",
